==History==
2024
*The Electro Dragon's Evolution [[Cards|card]] was added to the game on 7/10/2024, in the [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (7/10/2024)|October 2024 Update]].
*On 17/10/2024, a [[Version History#Maintenance Break (17/10/2024)|maintenance break]], fixed a bug where Evolved Electro Dragon did not chain into invisible [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]].
*On 16/12/2024, the [[Version History#2024 Quarter 4 Update (16/12/2024)|2024 Quarter 4 Update]], added a sound effect to the Evolved Electro Dragon after death. It also fixed various bugs with the Evolved Electro Dragon.
2025
*On 8/1/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (8/1/2025)|Balance Update]], decreased the Evolved Electro Dragon's damage after the first 3 chains by 33%.
*On 31/3/2025, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], decreased the Evolved Electro Dragon's hitpoints by 0.1%. It also made it so that Evolved Electro Dragon's boost from a [[Rune Giant]] would apply every third attack instead of every third hit in each attack.
2026

* On 2/3/2026, a Balance Update, increased the Evolved Electro Dragon's hitpoints by 5%, and also decreased it's chain damage by 50%.
* On 1/6/2026, a Balance Update, increased the Evolved Electro Dragon's hitpoints by 5%.

==Trivia== 
*The Electro Dragon resemble [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_dragon dragons from European cultures]. being reptilian legendary creatures, often depicted as winged, horned, and capable of breathing fire. However, the Electro Dragon breathes lightning bolts instead.
*The word "Electro" come from the Greek word "''ἤλεκτρον''" (elektron), meaning amber, referring to its electrostatic capabilities. Electricity was first detected through electric fish from as far back as 2750 BCE where Ancient Egyptian texts described them as the "protectors" of all other fish. At around 600 BCE, Thales of Miletus made a series of observations on static electricity, from which he believed that friction rendered amber magnetic, in contrast to minerals such as magnetite, which needed no rubbing. Thales was incorrect in believing the attraction was due to a magnetic effect, but later science would prove a link between magnetism and electricity. Electricity would remain little more than an intellectual curiosity for millennia until 1600, when the English scientist William Gilbert wrote ''De Magnete'', in which he made a careful study of electricity and magnetism, distinguishing the lodestone effect from static electricity produced by rubbing amber.
**The Electro Dragon is 1 of 3 evolved [[cards]] associated with electricity, with the others being [[Zap/Evolution|Zap]] and [[Tesla/Evolution|Tesla]].
***In the Spanish, Italian, Russian, Arabic, Portuguese, and Thai language settings of the game, the Electro Dragon's name translates to "Electric Dragon". In the Chinese and Finnish language settings of the game, the Electro Dragon's name translates to "Thunder Dragon" and "Lightning Dragon" respectively.
*The headwear the Evolved Electro Dragon has shows a resemblance to the Level 6 Electro Dragon from Clash of Clans.
*The Electro Dragon is 1 of 2 evolved [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that can deal damage to multiple units with one attack without an area damage radius, the other being [[Hunter/Evolution|Hunter]].
*The Electro Dragon’s Evolution is the subject of an [[Emotes|Emote]].
*Before the Electro Dragon Evolution's release, the Evolved Electro Dragon's projectile speed of the chain attack after 3 targets was decreased to 400 (from 500), and it was made so that the chain attack would no longer stun enemies after 3 targets.

